    "klt erc supply spec for the assembled ring (T1 item 11). Layer numbers are the sky130A GDS map used by layout/sky130_cells.py.",
    "Rails per spec CELL.5: VSS met5, VDDIO met4, VDD met3. Guard taps per CELL.8: p+ strip (VSS) and n-well/n+ strip (VDDIO).",
    "poly is declared only because stackup[0] must be the gate role; the ring draws no poly.",
    "devices[]: the supply clamp's MIM cap draws a via3 array on capm (89/44) between its met3 bottom plate and met4 top plate. Without the marker the stackup reads that array as a met3-met4 via and shorts the cap's two plates, which shorts VDD, VDDIO and VSS. The carve-out removes the array under capm from via3; it is a connectivity declaration, not a claim about the cap.",
    "The xhigh poly resistor bodies (66/13) are not carved out: they stay conducting, which is not a short between declared supplies, and carving them leaves each bar's floating T1 poly node as an erc.floating_gate.",
    "ties[]: the four clamp n-wells in the vdd cells (core PFETs, body on VDD) are listed as boxes in ring coordinates (um, one per rotation of the vdd cell). Regenerate them if the vdd cell or ring placement moves."
